    {
      "id": "3.7.9",
      "label": "3.7.9",
      "numbers": [
        9
      ],
      "devanagari": "प्रतीक्षमाणः त्वाम् एव न आरोहे अहम् महायशः |\nदेव लोकम् इतो वीर देहम् त्यक्त्वा महीतले\nचित्रकूटम् उपादाय राज्य भ्रष्टो असि मे श्रुतः |",
      "iast": "",
      "translation": "\"I am awaiting for you only, oh, greatly renowned one, without my ascent to heavens by casting off this body on the earth's plane, oh, brave one, for I have heard that you have arrived at Chitrakuta after you are repudiated from your kingdom...",
      "notes": [
        "This heaven ' <em>deva loka</em> heaven is negated for total salvation. Total salvation is at your tri-feet, <em>tridiva</em>. So 'I have not ascended to heavens, which causes rebirth after the decline of merit, thus I am waiting for your arrival for Total Salvation, moksha...' So said the sage to Rama. Govindaraja. \"You birthed in Raghu's dynasty for the elimination of Ravana, and also foregone your kingdom and you are coming this way. So I am waiting for your graceful look, without going to heavens leaving the body. Should I leave the body and go to heavens, I cannot see <em>parama puruṣa</em> , The Absolute, in you... so I did not cast off this body...' Thus said the sage to Rama. Maheshvara Tirtha."
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "mahaa yashaH",
          "iast": "mahā yaśaḥ",
          "devanagari": "महा यशः",
          "meaning": "greatly renowned",
