          "devanagari": "[इति",
          "meaning": "thus a]",
          "anvayaIndex": 7,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "me shrutaH",
          "iast": "me śrutaḥ",
          "devanagari": "मे श्रुतः",
          "meaning": "I heard thus.",
          "anvayaIndex": 8,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.7.10",
      "label": "3.7.10, 11",
      "numbers": [
        10,
        11
      ],
      "devanagari": "इह उपयातः काकुत्स्थः देवराजः शततक्रतुः\nउपागंय च मे देवो महादेवः सुर ईश्वरः |\nसर्वान् लोकान् जितान् आह मम पुण्येन कर्मणा",
      "iast": "",
      "translation": "\"The king of gods and the chief invitee in hundred sacrifices Indra approached me, and that great deity said me that I have conquered all the worlds by my meritorious deeds...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "kaakutsthaH",
          "iast": "kākutsthaḥ",
          "devanagari": "काकुत्स्थः",
          "meaning": "Rama",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "shata kratuH deva rajaH iha upayaataH",
          "iast": "śata kratuḥ deva rajaḥ iha upayātaḥ",
          "devanagari": "शत क्रतुः देव रजः इह उपयातः",
          "meaning": "one with hundred rituals, deities, king, here, he came",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mahaadevaH sura iishvaraH",
          "iast": "mahādevaḥ sura īśvaraḥ",
          "devanagari": "महादेवः सुर ईश्वरः",
          "meaning": "great god, celestials'",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "devaH",
          "iast": "devaḥ",
          "devanagari": "देवः",
          "meaning": "such Indra",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "upaagamya",
          "iast": "upāgamya",
          "devanagari": "उपागम्य",
          "meaning": "on approaching",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mama puNyena karmaNaa",
          "iast": "mama puṇyena karmaṇā",
          "devanagari": "मम पुण्येन कर्मणा",
          "meaning": "by my, meritorious, deeds",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sarvaan lokaan jitaan",
          "iast": "sarvān lokān jitān",
          "devanagari": "सर्वान् लोकान् जितान्",
          "meaning": "all, worlds, conquered [ by me]",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "maam aaha",
          "iast": "mām āha",
          "devanagari": "मां आह",
          "meaning": "[thus] to me, he said.",
          "anvayaIndex": 7,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.7.12",
      "label": "3.7.12",
      "numbers": [
        12
      ],
      "devanagari": "तेषु देव ऋषि जुष्टेषु जितेशु तपसा मया |\nमत् प्रसादात् स भार्यः त्वम् विहरस्व स लक्ष्मणः",
      "iast": "",
      "translation": "\"Let me bequeath those worlds that are cherished by gods and sages alike, but which are won over by me by my ascesis, and you enjoy in them with your wife and with your brother Lakshmana...",
      "notes": [
        "This sage Suteekshna too is dedicating all his merit accrued by his penance at the feet of Vishnu. This is the same effort of dedication, which Sage Sharabhanga offered, to Rama at 3-5-33 of this canto. Any thing accrued by human effort and energy, if dedicated at the feet of god, is doubly meritorious and establishes a selflessness of the devotee. Even in any daily worship it will be concluded with a saying, <em>ye tat phalam parameśvara arpaṇamastu...</em> i.e., whatever is the result of this worship it is dedicated in the Supreme..."
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "mayaa tapasaa jiteSu deva R^iSi juSTeSu",
          "iast": "mayā tapasā jiteṣu deva ṛṣi juṣṭeṣu",
          "devanagari": "मया तपसा जितेषु देव ऋषि जुष्टेषु",
          "meaning": "by me, by ascesis, won over, by gods and sages, cherished",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "teSu",
          "iast": "teṣu",
          "devanagari": "तेषु",
          "meaning": "in them [those conquered worlds]",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sa bhaaryaH",
          "iast": "sa bhāryaḥ",
          "devanagari": "स भार्यः",
          "meaning": "with, your wife",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sa lakshmanaH",
          "iast": "sa lakśmanaḥ",
          "devanagari": "स लक्श्मनः",
          "meaning": "with, Lakshmana",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tvam mat prasaadaat viharasva",
          "iast": "tvam mat prasādāt viharasva",
          "devanagari": "त्वं मत् प्रसादात् विहरस्व",
          "meaning": "you, by my, bequeathal, you enjoy.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.7.13",
      "label": "3.7.13",
      "numbers": [
        13
      ],
      "devanagari": "तम् उग्र तपसम् दीप्तम् महर्षिम् सत्य वादिनम् |\nप्रत्युवाच आत्मवान् रामो ब्रह्माणम् इव वासवः",
      "iast": "",
      "translation": "That self-respecting Rama replied the radiant sage with intense asceticism, a great soul and an advocate of truth by himself, as Indra would reply to Brahma.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "aatmavaan",
          "iast": "ātmavān",
          "devanagari": "आत्मवान्",
          "meaning": "self-respecting one",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "ugra tapasaa diiptam",
          "iast": "ugra tapasā dīptam",
          "devanagari": "उग्र तपसा दीप्तं",
          "meaning": "by intense, asceticism, radiant one",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tam",
          "iast": "tam",
          "devanagari": "तं",
          "meaning": "him",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "maharSim",
          "iast": "maharṣim",
          "devanagari": "महर्षिं",
          "meaning": "to great sage",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "satya vaadinam",
          "iast": "satya vādinam",
          "devanagari": "सत्य वादिनं",
          "meaning": "truth, advocate of",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "prati uvaaca",
          "iast": "prati uvāca",
          "devanagari": "प्रति उवाच",
          "meaning": "in turn, said",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "brahmaaNam iva vaasavaH",
          "iast": "brahmāṇam iva vāsavaḥ",
          "devanagari": "ब्रह्माणं इव वासवः",
          "meaning": "to Brahma, like, Indra.",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.7.14",
      "label": "3.7.14",
      "numbers": [
        14
      ],
      "devanagari": "अहम् एव आहरिष्यामि स्वयम् लोकान् महामुने |\nआवासम् तु अहम् इच्छामि प्रदिष्टम् इह कानने",
      "iast": "",
      "translation": "\"I alone can gain all those worlds, oh, great saint, I now seek a place to dwell here in this forest as indicated by you...",
      "notes": [
        "This is the same situation with Sage Sharabhanga in the 5th chapter of this canto. This is an allusive saying by Rama. cf. 3-5-33."
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "mahaamune",
          "iast": "mahāmune",
          "devanagari": "महामुने",
          "meaning": "oh, great saint",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "aham eva aaharishyaami svayam",
          "iast": "aham eva āhariśyāmi svayam",
          "devanagari": "अहं एव आहरिश्यामि स्वयं",
          "meaning": "I, alone, will gain, myself",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "lokaan",
          "iast": "lokān",
          "devanagari": "लोकान्",
          "meaning": "all worlds",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "aavasam tu",
          "iast": "āvasam tu",
          "devanagari": "आवसं तु",
          "meaning": "dwelling place, only",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "aham icChaami",
          "iast": "aham icchāmi",
          "devanagari": "अहं इच्छामि",
          "meaning": "I seek",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "pradiSTam iha kaanane",
          "iast": "pradiṣṭam iha kānane",
          "devanagari": "प्रदिष्टं इह कानने",
          "meaning": "indicated [by you,] here, in this forest.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.7.15",
      "label": "3.7.15",
      "numbers": [
        15
      ],
      "devanagari": "भवान् सर्वत्र कुशलः सर्वभूत हिते रतः |\nआख्यातः शरभंगेन गौतमेन महात्मना",
      "iast": "",
      "translation": "\"You are an expert in all affairs, and you are interested in the welfare of all the beings, so said the great souled Sage Sharabhanga of Sage Gautama's dynasty...\" [So said Rama to the sage.]",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "bhavaan sarvatra kushalaH",
          "iast": "bhavān sarvatra kuśalaḥ",
          "devanagari": "भवान् सर्वत्र कुशलः",
          "meaning": "you are, in all affairs, expert",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sarva bhuuta hiteH rataH",
          "iast": "sarva bhūta hiteḥ rataḥ",
          "devanagari": "सर्व भूत हितेः रतः",
          "meaning": "all, beings', welfare, interested in",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "aakhyaataH mahaatmanaa",
          "iast": "ākhyātaḥ mahātmanā",
          "devanagari": "आख्यातः महात्मना",
          "meaning": "sharabhangena gautamena = said by, great soul, Sharabhanga, belonging to sage Gautama's dynasty.",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.7.16",
      "label": "3.7.16",
      "numbers": [
        16
      ],
      "devanagari": "एवम् उक्तः तु रामेण महर्षिः लोक विश्रुतः |\nअब्रवीत् मधुरम् वाक्यम् हर्षेण महता युतः",
      "iast": "",
      "translation": "When said thus by Rama, that great sage with world renown spoke sweet worded sentence with great pleasure.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "raameNa evam uktaH",
          "iast": "rāmeṇa evam uktaḥ",
          "devanagari": "रामेण एवं उक्तः",
          "meaning": "by Rama, that way, when said",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "loka vishrutaH maharSiH",
          "iast": "loka viśrutaḥ maharṣiḥ",
          "devanagari": "लोक विश्रुतः महर्षिः",
          "meaning": "world, renowned, sage",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mahataa harSeNa yutaH",
          "iast": "mahatā harṣeṇa yutaḥ",
          "devanagari": "महता हर्षेण युतः",
          "meaning": "with great, joy, having",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "abraviit madhuram vaakyam",
          "iast": "abravīt madhuram vākyam",
          "devanagari": "अब्रवीत् मधुरं वाक्यं",
          "meaning": "spoke, sweet worded, sentence.",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.7.17",
      "label": "3.7.17",
      "numbers": [
        17
      ],
      "devanagari": "अयम् एव आश्रमो राम गुणवान् रंयताम् इति |\nऋषि संघ अनुचरितः सदा मूल फलैर् युतः",
      "iast": "",
      "translation": "\"You can take delight in this good featured hermitage alone, for groups of sages will always be moving here, and this always contains tubers and fruits...\" Thus said Sage Suteekshna.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "R^ishi sangha anu charitaH",
          "iast": "ṛśi sangha anu caritaḥ",
          "devanagari": "ऋशि सन्घ अनु चरितः",
          "meaning": "sage, groups, well, moving about",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sadaa muula phalaiH yutaH",
          "iast": "sadā mūla phalaiḥ yutaḥ",
          "devanagari": "सदा मूल फलैः युतः",
          "meaning": "always, tubers, fruits, containing in",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "ayam aashramaH eva guNavaan",
          "iast": "ayam āśramaḥ eva guṇavān",
          "devanagari": "अयं आश्रमः एव गुणवान्",
          "meaning": "this, hermitage, alone, fully featured one",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "ramyataam iti",
          "iast": "ramyatām iti",
          "devanagari": "रम्यतां इति",
          "meaning": "delight here, thus.",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.7.18",
      "label": "3.7.18",
      "numbers": [
        18
      ],
      "devanagari": "इमम् आश्रमम् आगंय मृग संघा महीयसः |\nअहत्वा प्रतिगच्छन्ति लोभयित्वा अकुतोभयाः",
      "iast": "",
      "translation": "\"But herds of very large animals will be coming to this hermitage, they return after scaring us, of course without killing anyone, and they fear none...",
      "notes": [
        "There is something in this verse. Some translations read <em>mṛga</em> as deer, while some others read it as animals. If they are just deer, the word <em>a + hatvā</em> , without killing, is of no use, for deer is not a carnivorous animal to kill someone. In other versions, this verse is a complete recast telling that herds of great size animals come and blare, but do not kill or fear any one. Even if it were so, this sage has got a tolerance for them too. And if some latent meaning is picked up, the large herds of deer, moving as they like in this hermitage, are said to be 'luring' the sages, <em>lobhayitbvā</em>. A presumption arises here. This must be the same 'lure' Seetha got on seeing Golden Deer. But Rama raises his bow and arrow to kill these animals that disturb tranquillity of hermitage, whether it be deer or other blaring wild animals. So Rama's fury must be at the 'luring deer', say Golden Deer, but not at ordinary deer. Thus this usage of 'deer and lure' may be taken as <em>lakśaṇa</em> for <em>lakśita</em> of Ramayana."
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "imam aashramam aagamya",
          "iast": "imam āśramam āgamya",
          "devanagari": "इमं आश्रमं आगम्य",
          "meaning": "to this hermitage, having come",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mR^iga sanghaa mahiiyasaH",
          "iast": "mṛga sanghā mahīyasaḥ",
          "devanagari": "मृग सन्घा महीयसः",
          "meaning": "deer, herds, large ones",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "a hatvaa prati gacChanti",
          "iast": "a hatvā prati gacchanti",
          "devanagari": "अ हत्वा प्रति गच्छन्ति",
          "meaning": "without killing, return they go",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "lobhayitvaa",
          "iast": "lobhayitvā",
          "devanagari": "लोभयित्वा",
          "meaning": "luring us",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "a kutaH bhayaaH",
          "iast": "a kutaḥ bhayāḥ",
          "devanagari": "अ कुतः भयाः",
          "meaning": "not, from anyone, fearing [fearing none.]",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.7.19",
      "label": "3.7.19",
      "numbers": [
        19
      ],
      "devanagari": "ना अन्यो दोषो भवेत् अत्र मृगेभ्यः अन्यत्र विद्धि वै |\nतत् श्रुत्वा वचनम् तस्य महर्षेः लक्ष्मणाग्रजः\nउवाच वचनम् धीरो विगृह्य स शरम् धनुः |",
      "iast": "",
      "translation": "\"Know that no other problem is there other than the animals...\" So said the sage. On hearing those words of that great sage, that brave elder brother of Lakshmana taking bow and arrow said this sentence.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "viddhi vai",
          "iast": "viddhi vai",
          "devanagari": "विद्धि वै",
          "meaning": "you know, thus indeed",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "atra mR^igebhyaH anyatra anya doSaH naa bhavet",
          "iast": "atra mṛgebhyaḥ anyatra anya doṣaḥ nā bhavet",
          "devanagari": "अत्र मृगेभ्यः अन्यत्र अन्य दोषः ना भवेत्",
          "meaning": "here, from animals, other than, other, problem, will not, be there",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "dhiiraH lakshmamaNa agrajaH",
          "iast": "dhīraḥ lakśmamaṇa agrajaḥ",
          "devanagari": "धीरः लक्श्ममण अग्रजः",
          "meaning": "couraeous one, Lakshmana's, elder - Rama",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tasya maharsheH tat vacanam shrutvaa",
          "iast": "tasya maharśeḥ tat vacanam śrutvā",
          "devanagari": "तस्य महर्शेः तत् वचनं श्रुत्वा",
          "meaning": "of that, great sage, that, sentence, on hearing",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sa sharam dhanuH vi gR^ihya",
          "iast": "sa śaram dhanuḥ vi gṛhya",
          "devanagari": "स शरं धनुः वि गृह्य",
          "meaning": "with, arrow, bow, on taking",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "uvaaca vacanam",
          "iast": "uvāca vacanam",
          "devanagari": "उवाच वचनं",
          "meaning": "said, sentence.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.7.20",
      "label": "3.7.20",
      "numbers": [
        20
      ],
      "devanagari": "तान् अहम् सुमहाभाग मृगसंघान् समागतान्\nहन्याम् निशित धारेण शरेण नत पर्वणा |",
      "iast": "",
      "translation": "\"I will eradicate them, oh, greatly blessed one, those animals that will come collectively in herds with sharp edged, curve-end arrows...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "su mahaa bhaagaH",
          "iast": "su mahā bhāgaḥ",
          "devanagari": "सु महा भागः",
          "meaning": "oh, greatly, blessed one",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "samaagataan taan mR^iga sanghaan",
          "iast": "samāgatān tān mṛga sanghān",
